{"title":"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8_(Integral_Calculus,_not_rigorous)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8 (Integral Calculus, not rigorous)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_9_(Telescoping)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 9 (Telescoping)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/a/15aa49f8e9ec05944ab2d5b707486ee1f38e1793.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{\\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\cos n^\\circ}{\\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -39px\" width=\"110\" height=\"87\" />. What is the greatest integer that does not exceed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/6/f8601c23e7ea6708da2f181ae49156648df382ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"37\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/f/79f604f50fcfe471104e0f1ec380f6b982a7d2d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\cos n}{\\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n} = \\frac{\\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\cos n}{\\sum_{n=46}^{89} \\cos n} = \\frac {\\cos 1 + \\cos 2 + \\dots + \\cos 44}{\\cos 89 + \\cos 88 + \\dots + \\cos 46}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"465\" height=\"51\" /> by the cofunction identities.(We could have also written it as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9fe5c16f86a3a45ffcf12e5ae0ce0f70d82d6159.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\cos n}{\\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n} = \\frac{\\sum_{n=46}^{89} \\sin n}{\\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n} = \\frac {\\sin 89 + \\sin 88 + \\dots + \\sin 46}{\\sin 1 + \\sin 2 + \\dots + \\sin 44}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"457\" height=\"51\" />.)\n</p><p>Now use the sum-product formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/4/81460d064d4f51ce062d6e96cb8062f02db5b8cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos x + \\cos y = 2\\cos\\left(\\frac{x+y}{2}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{x-y}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"338\" height=\"45\" /> \nWe want to pair up <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e45772945ac6569ae26fcc813c5d8b303719318d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[1, 44]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/9/7e96e650e4cf269321dd4171176a63babd2bfe26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[2, 43]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/211be085358dc41b04e7b1c2b420d83f9f8290f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[3, 42]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, etc. from the numerator and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/b/f0bb1a6b9d5a32bcae7fd03ec7520de35cc8cceb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[46, 89]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/f/ebf5d863e9c99bb2cd44774ecf2d76e262f63201.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[47, 88]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/c/04cc0daa71877ad651dd786c37477df71ac1a3bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[48, 87]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> etc. from the denominator. Then we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/c/95c0c2cfe801942ce97b4e91d93874da5b786d1d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\cos n}{\\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n} = \\frac{\\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\cos n}{\\sum_{n=46}^{89} \\cos n} = \\frac{2\\cos(\\frac{45}{2})[\\cos(\\frac{43}{2})+\\cos(\\frac{41}{2})+\\dots+\\cos(\\frac{1}{2})]}{2\\cos(\\frac{135}{2})[\\cos(\\frac{43}{2})+\\cos(\\frac{41}{2})+\\dots+\\cos(\\frac{1}{2})]} \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\cos(\\frac{45}{2})}{\\cos(\\frac{135}{2})}\\]\" width=\"662\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>To calculate this number, use the half angle formula. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/5/e55e33a44d2bdce7753ab2dd53210f83f11d09f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right) = \\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{\\cos x + 1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"194\" height=\"45\" />, then our number becomes: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/0/080c7871943d54388c9e82e6a8ff94507d80a50d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sqrt{\\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + 1}{2}}}{\\sqrt{\\frac{\\frac{-\\sqrt{2}}{2} + 1}{2}}}\\]\" width=\"66\" height=\"70\" /> in which we drop the negative roots (as it is clear cosine of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/d/91d413c0964b8ba3371f882fd21fa87baeb74e92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22.5$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/3/f23ce85fe560e63e3f0771d2f703a94450c0d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$67.5$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> are positive). We can easily simplify this:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bd0284ce082450be926f632693a7bb4ca81f730.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*} \\frac{\\sqrt{\\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + 1}{2}}}{\\sqrt{\\frac{\\frac{-\\sqrt{2}}{2} + 1}{2}}} &amp;=&amp; \\sqrt{\\frac{\\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{4}}{\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{4}}} \\\\ &amp;=&amp; \\sqrt{\\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{2-\\sqrt{2}}} \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{2+\\sqrt{2}}} \\\\ &amp;=&amp; \\sqrt{\\frac{(2+\\sqrt{2})^2}{2}} \\\\ &amp;=&amp; \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ &amp;=&amp; \\sqrt{2}+1 \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"284\" height=\"269\" />\n</p><p>And hence our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/e/deeeae569adc3156f1e14b8f3144a4c68a66e4c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor 100x \\rfloor =  \\lfloor 100(1 + \\sqrt {2}) \\rfloor = \\boxed{241}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"254\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/f/60f0bc4345e93f98e085d69df243e20c21687bce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*} x &amp;=&amp; \\frac {\\sum_{n = 1}^{44} \\cos n^\\circ}{\\sum_{n = 1}^{44} \\sin n^\\circ} = \\frac {\\cos 1 + \\cos 2 + \\dots + \\cos 44}{\\sin 1 + \\sin 2 + \\dots + \\sin 44}\\\\ &amp;=&amp; \\frac {\\cos (45 - 1) + \\cos(45 - 2) + \\dots + \\cos(45 - 44)}{\\sin 1 + \\sin 2 + \\dots + \\sin 44} \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"420\" height=\"95\" />\n</p><p>Using the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f561e3221de67ab6ecaf63ee2d41cfdb3ba2055.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin a + \\sin b = 2\\sin \\frac{a+b}2 \\cos \\frac{a-b}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"268\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/d/91d35fb99675e99629f016b967f2317f19cec717.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Longrightarrow \\sin x + \\cos x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"129\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/0/de06339d1e6c7ada6df7a6a880acdaac2f9e8a3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\sin x + \\sin (90-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0af75ddc965791c3a4837e5dd1c25636c64f3345.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 2 \\sin 45 \\cos (45-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"165\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/f/c4f2ca60f0e22f52071f166a5c13a9c682663386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\sqrt{2} \\cos (45-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"21\" />, that <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Summation\" title=\"Summation\">summation</a> reduces to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/6/e669d8983303235b5cbe64d3a70d19c9a7032642.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*}x &amp;=&amp; \\left(\\frac {1}{\\sqrt {2}}\\right)\\left(\\frac {(\\cos 1 + \\cos2 + \\dots + \\cos44) + (\\sin1 + \\sin2 + \\dots + \\sin44)}{\\sin1 + \\sin2 + \\dots + \\sin44}\\right)\\\\ &amp;=&amp; \\left(\\frac {1}{\\sqrt {2}}\\right)\\left(1 + \\frac {\\cos 1 + \\cos 2 + \\dots + \\cos 44}{\\sin 1 + \\sin 2 + \\dots + \\sin 44}\\right) \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"598\" height=\"92\" />\n</p><p>This fraction is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.  Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/d/ded1ad834c78f695357f886f995671ba6bca4336.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*} x &amp;=&amp; \\left(\\frac {1}{\\sqrt {2}}\\right)\\left(1 + x\\right)\\\\ \\frac {1}{\\sqrt {2}} &amp;=&amp; x\\left(\\frac {\\sqrt {2} - 1}{\\sqrt {2}}\\right)\\\\ x &amp;=&amp; \\frac {1}{\\sqrt {2} - 1} = 1 + \\sqrt {2}\\\\ \\lfloor 100x \\rfloor &amp;=&amp; \\lfloor 100(1 + \\sqrt {2}) \\rfloor = \\boxed{241}\\\\ \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"274\" height=\"180\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A slight variant of the above solution, note that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/6/3f622a969ef566260edfef101ed2afd764c47014.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*} \\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\cos n + \\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n &amp;=&amp; \\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n + \\sin(90-n)\\\\ &amp;=&amp; \\sqrt{2}\\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\cos(45-n) = \\sqrt{2}\\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\cos n\\\\ \\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n &amp;=&amp; (\\sqrt{2}-1)\\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\cos n \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"465\" height=\"170\" />\n</p><p>This is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ratio\" title=\"Ratio\">ratio</a> we are looking for. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> reduces to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/c/c4c13b6c1f3c26e657c659a0e150830ef7c5d677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2} - 1} = \\sqrt{2} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"138\" height=\"41\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/b/79be811d8d4f0ecaf0c8faefaf29670830fe6d5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor 100(\\sqrt{2} + 1)\\rfloor = \\boxed{241}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"176\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/0/900700405bafd4f43a481dd4199bfa2d1a762756.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{n = 1}^{44} \\text{cis } n^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"70\" height=\"50\" />. The fraction is given by the real part divided by the imaginary part.\n</p><p>The sum can be written <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc629d83028dd3c58154f92913339a2b74e89717.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$- 1 + \\sum_{n = 0}^{44} \\text{cis } n^\\circ = - 1 + \\frac {\\text{cis } 45^\\circ - 1}{\\text{cis } 1^\\circ - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"270\" height=\"50\" /> (by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=De_Moivre%27s_Theorem\" title=\"De Moivre&#39;s Theorem\">De Moivre's Theorem</a> with geometric series)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/7/dc7b3e035eb51215e2a10a78912f36fb5d51c3b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= - 1 + \\frac {\\frac {\\sqrt {2}}{2} - 1 + \\frac {i \\sqrt {2}}{2}}{\\text{cis } 1^\\circ - 1} = - 1 + \\frac {\\left( \\frac {\\sqrt {2}}{2} - 1 + \\frac {i \\sqrt {2}}{2} \\right) (\\text{cis } ( - 1^\\circ) - 1)}{(\\cos 1^\\circ - 1)^2 + \\sin^2 1^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"482\" height=\"57\" /> (after multiplying by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complex_conjugate\" title=\"Complex conjugate\">complex conjugate</a>)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/3/fb382b7f8c0fec0ddda28c714cb2b9337012ec42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= - 1 + \\frac {\\left( \\frac {\\sqrt {2}}{2} - 1 \\right) (\\cos 1^\\circ - 1) + \\frac {\\sqrt {2}}{2}\\sin 1^\\circ + i\\left( \\left(1 - \\frac {\\sqrt {2}}{2} \\right) \\sin 1^\\circ + \\frac {\\sqrt {2}}{2} (\\cos 1^\\circ - 1)\\right)}{2(1 - \\cos 1^\\circ)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"627\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3ab2ebd6ebec745250e8383c011f1d8bdd1dca8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= - \\frac {1}{2} - \\frac {\\sqrt {2}}{4} - \\frac {i\\sqrt {2}}{4} + \\frac {\\sin 1^\\circ \\left( \\frac {\\sqrt {2}}{2} + i\\left( 1 - \\frac {\\sqrt {2}}{2} \\right) \\right)}{2(1 - \\cos 1^\\circ)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"371\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p>Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trigonometric_identities\" title=\"Trigonometric identities\">tangent half-angle formula</a>, this becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/9/8c971541d2b2ef0497e673ec70da35a77ad8256e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( - \\frac {1}{2} + \\frac {\\sqrt {2}}{4}[\\cot (1/2^\\circ) - 1] \\right) + i\\left( \\frac {1}{2}\\cot (1/2^\\circ) - \\frac {\\sqrt {2}}{4}[\\cot (1/2^\\circ) + 1] \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"530\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>Dividing the two parts and multiplying each part by 4, the fraction is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/6/046eafcfd8c350b5e535513cb52121d21dea133e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac { - 2 + \\sqrt {2}[\\cot (1/2^\\circ) - 1]}{2\\cot (1/2^\\circ) - \\sqrt {2}[\\cot (1/2^\\circ) + 1]}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"249\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>Although an exact value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/f/2afdf5cea5580fa79518bd8e356afd8905cfc0a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot (1/2^\\circ)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> in terms of radicals will be difficult, this is easily known: it is really large!\n</p><p>So treat it as though it were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/7/b671f1bb7e4ee86584347d5d22f1dc8abdb5bef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"9\" />. The fraction is approximated by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/1/da1ca9d2eb0ebdd9725f5cb51460c55bdf51e943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {\\sqrt {2}}{2 - \\sqrt {2}} = \\frac {\\sqrt {2}(2 + \\sqrt {2})}{2} = 1 + \\sqrt {2}\\Rightarrow \\lfloor 100(1+\\sqrt2)\\rfloor=\\boxed{241}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"466\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/0/900700405bafd4f43a481dd4199bfa2d1a762756.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{n = 1}^{44} \\text{cis } n^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"70\" height=\"50\" />. The fraction is given by the real part divided by the imaginary part.\n</p><p>The sum can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be0ce46e771367fa4b979a9de00ec1a8ecc3feef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{n=1}^{22} (\\text{cis } n^\\circ + \\text{cis } 45-n^\\circ)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"186\" height=\"50\" />. \nConsider the rhombus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b91381b367f9753ded66ab981c7451f2cb117578.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OABC$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> on the complex plane such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the origin, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> represents <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/0/b2044dab4df62f31b53768c0e25531a9b78f3ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis } n^\\circ$\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> represents <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/2/9924b71d8a27843f43c9ef4be41634d27043a97f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis } n^\\circ + \\text{cis } 45-n^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"146\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> represents <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/0/b2044dab4df62f31b53768c0e25531a9b78f3ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis } n^\\circ$\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />. Simple geometry shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a082167d1f9b7470be9c5ca9cc9daf79af57f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BOA = 22.5-k^\\circ$\" width=\"150\" height=\"13\" />, so the angle that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/2/9924b71d8a27843f43c9ef4be41634d27043a97f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis } n^\\circ + \\text{cis } 45-n^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"146\" height=\"14\" /> makes with the real axis is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/a/eea5c06f0a939dc4e3d874948a0659e799845923.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22.5^\\circ$\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be0ce46e771367fa4b979a9de00ec1a8ecc3feef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{n=1}^{22} (\\text{cis } n^\\circ + \\text{cis } 45-n^\\circ)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"186\" height=\"50\" /> is the sum of collinear complex numbers, so the angle the sum makes with the real axis is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/a/eea5c06f0a939dc4e3d874948a0659e799845923.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22.5^\\circ$\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />. So our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/8/7a89102a41eb1a8be9b83d526a585c5ef18a2728.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor 100 \\cot(22.5^\\circ) \\rfloor = \\boxed{241}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"188\" height=\"23\" />. \n</p><p>Note that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/2627fb12f44f659dd924c366e7427becad51941b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot(22.5^\\circ) = \\sqrt2 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"21\" /> can be shown easily through half-angle formula.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3e429216f54284a569e505f81ccbde090bb8d66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x =\\frac{\\sum_{n=46}^{89} \\sin n^{\\circ}}{\\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"135\" height=\"49\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0b6fcd63dc0e70eb72bb7888a485882d456fe82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos x = \\sin (90^{\\circ}-x).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" /> Now, by the sine angle sum, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/5/fd5c3afb5eb407acdfadfbddbb956fad600012cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin (x+45^{\\circ}) = \\sin 45^{\\circ}(\\sin x + \\cos x).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"283\" height=\"18\" /> So the expression simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f014868fc8f3ef826967a7ae2909faf85551b772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin 45^{\\circ}\\left(\\frac{\\sum_{n=1}^{44} (\\sin n^{\\circ}+\\cos n^{\\circ})}{\\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n^{\\circ}}\\right) = \\sin 45^{\\circ}\\left(1+\\frac{\\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\cos n^{\\circ}}{\\sum_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n^{\\circ}}\\right)=\\sin 45^{\\circ}(1+x).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"627\" height=\"53\" /> Therefore we have the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/a/28a545a6314a6498d9f4a0249c8a37616c9e98ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\sin 45^{\\circ}(1+x) \\implies x = \\sqrt{2}+1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"284\" height=\"21\" /> Finishing, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/0/100a28f00f324ad3643bcb699783ed68e76325aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor 100x \\rfloor = \\boxed{241}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"124\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can pair the terms of the summations as below. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/3/5b3802773e1044d5c650f83277c919f9ff4f1d94.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{(\\cos{1} + \\cos{44}) + (\\cos{2} + \\cos{43}) + (\\cos{3} + \\cos{42}) + \\cdots + (\\cos{22} + \\cos{23})}{(\\sin{1} + \\sin{44}) + (\\sin{2} + \\sin{43}) + (\\sin{3} + \\sin{42}) + \\cdots + (\\sin{22} + \\sin{23})}.\\]\" width=\"598\" height=\"43\" />  \n</p><p>From here, we use the cosine and sine subtraction formulas as shown. \n</p><p>\\begin{align*}\n&amp;\\dfrac{(\\cos(45-44) + \\cos(45-1)) + (\\cos(45-43) + \\cos(45-2))+ \\cdots (\\cos(45-23) + \\cos(45-22))}{(\\sin(45-44) + \\sin(45-1)) + (\\sin(45-43) + \\sin(45-2))+ \\cdots (\\sin(45-23) + \\sin(45-22))} \\\\  \n&amp;= \\dfrac{(\\cos{45}\\cos{44} +\\sin{45}\\sin{44} + \\cos{45}\\cos{1} + \\sin{45}\\sin{1})+ \\cdots + (\\cos{45}\\cos{23} + \\sin{45}\\sin{23} + \\cos{45}\\cos{22} + \\sin{45}\\sin{22})}{(\\sin{45}\\cos{44}-\\cos{45}\\sin{44} + \\sin{45}\\cos{1} - \\cos{45}\\sin{1}) + \\cdots + (\\sin{45}\\cos{23} -\\cos{45}\\sin{23} + \\sin{45}\\cos{22} - \\cos{45}\\sin{22})} \\\\ \n&amp;= \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}/2(\\cos{44} + \\sin{44} + \\cos{1}+\\sin{1} +\\cos{43} + \\sin{43} + \\cos{2} + \\sin{2} + \\cdots + \\cos{23} + \\sin{23} + \\cos{22} + \\sin{22})}{\\sqrt{2}/2(\\cos{44} -\\sin{44} +\\cos{1} - \\sin{1} + \\cos{43}-\\sin{43} + \\cos{2} -\\sin{2} +\\cdots + \\cos{23}-\\sin{23} + \\cos{22} - \\sin{22})} \\\\ \n&amp;=\\dfrac{\\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\cos n^\\circ + \\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n^\\circ}{\\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\cos n^\\circ - \\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n^\\circ}. \n\\end{align*} \n</p><p>Since all of these operations have been performed to ensure equality, we can set the final line of the above mess equal to our original expression. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/ace2a85a7ea48e8858b43adf709600db48d1eac0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{\\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\cos n^\\circ + \\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n^\\circ}{\\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\cos n^\\circ - \\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n^\\circ} = \\frac{\\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\cos n^\\circ}{\\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n^\\circ}.\\]\" width=\"276\" height=\"87\" /> \n</p><p>For the sake of clarity, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/1/8a12f40078f262d2a4a05f8739c26a5f366e0b3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\cos n^\\circ = C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"115\" height=\"55\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/376da748749d75f3aac44839e46239235bf53594.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n^\\circ = S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"111\" height=\"55\" />. Then, we have \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/3/9b3b53704fce716e2886d65e7838f598ff3918b0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{C+S}{C-S} = \\dfrac{C}{S} \\implies CS+S^2 = C^2-CS.\\]\" width=\"308\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Finishing, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/8/f18c06e4040d02e8af629725aa7feccfdd24cd29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S^2+2CS=C^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />. Adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/6/f6631184ccb7a9018368c278608dea91f2f82ac5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> to both sides gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/f/06f370cb0db27bf57cbeb7895f138e1a72f9759f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(C+S)^2 = 2C^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"21\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/d/d7d18c42a67c089df15d73943885d4c7b228612b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C+S = \\pm C\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"21\" />. Taking the positive case gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/d/71df955ccc64ea2a21f38f61ea1fc7dc6e43ca3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S= C(\\sqrt{2}-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"24\" />. Finally, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/f/18f06e41c27b33ef02f01abb9d613c14cb5a2310.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=\\frac{\\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\cos n^\\circ}{\\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n^\\circ} = \\dfrac{C}{S} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1} = \\sqrt{2} +1 \\implies \\lfloor{100x\\rfloor} = \\boxed{241}.\\]\" width=\"488\" height=\"87\" /> \n</p><p>~NTfish\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_8_.28Integral_Calculus.2C_not_rigorous.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8_(Integral_Calculus,_not_rigorous)\">Solution 8 (Integral Calculus, not rigorous)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8 (Integral Calculus, not rigorous)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because the numerator and denominator are both sums, we can replace each with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b45828f292e161290be6ee62bc4c9df081ee1e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times the average (i.e. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic_mean\" title=\"Arithmetic mean\">arithmetic mean</a>) of the terms of the respective sums. These <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b45828f292e161290be6ee62bc4c9df081ee1e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />s will cancel out, leaving simply the ratio of the averages of the respective sums.\n</p><p>Given that the sums span from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/24335a00767ec09fb07068d2416faac7e83d1b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^{\\circ}\\approx 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> radians to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/3/cf301a374e8427d37650a0a205cc6578bb633f5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44^{\\circ}\\approx \\tfrac\\pi4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"64\" height=\"21\" /> radians, we would expect the average heights of cosine and sine on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8459b711fe8ec59f540becec4bbbc8d8a643654b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,\\tfrac\\pi4]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"41\" height=\"22\" /> to be very close if not equal to the given ratio. We can use definite <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integrals\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Integrals\">integrals</a> to calculate these averages.\n</p><p>The average height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11f986c49f29d7a2ed4c28cab7319fa2ee3ee978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos x$\" width=\"37\" height=\"8\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8459b711fe8ec59f540becec4bbbc8d8a643654b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,\\tfrac\\pi4]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"41\" height=\"22\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/e/0beb106bc44316149fa4c08a939c4d2fd9f2e6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac1{\\pi/4}\\int^{\\pi/4}_0(\\cos x) dx = \\frac4\\pi(\\sin\\frac\\pi4-\\sin0) = \\frac4\\pi\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt2}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"381\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>Similarly, the average height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e8f3a072de64627a11a2df663e577eb43d60c77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8459b711fe8ec59f540becec4bbbc8d8a643654b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,\\tfrac\\pi4]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"41\" height=\"22\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/5/9e59b6233d3400edfc8cd3dbb52ac8ff9e1664d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac1{\\pi/4}\\int^{\\pi/4}_0(\\sin x) dx = \\frac4\\pi(-\\cos\\frac\\pi4+\\cos0) = \\frac4\\pi\\cdot(1-\\frac{\\sqrt2}2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"446\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>Taking the ratio of these two values yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbc69887d4bd2eb8995cb3ccf4c9c62eacaf19cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt2/2}{1-\\sqrt2/2}=\\frac1{\\sqrt2-1}\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt2+1}{\\sqrt2+1}=\\frac{\\sqrt2+1}{2-1}=\\sqrt2+1 \\approx 1.41+1 = 2.41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"544\" height=\"50\" />. Thus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/2/3525a515bec36a712828edd9e5a770cacf178507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{241}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_9_.28Telescoping.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_9_(Telescoping)\">Solution 9 (Telescoping)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 9 (Telescoping)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89f7afb3d0805f78a60602a30c359101bd37769f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{\\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\cos n^\\circ}{\\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n^\\circ}=\\frac{\\sum\\limits_{n=46}^{89} \\sin n^\\circ}{\\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -42px\" width=\"221\" height=\"93\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe29a68798e0aa8d9b65a2493dc5a43db942e918.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{\\sum\\limits_{n=46}^{89} \\sin n^\\circ\\sin0.5^\\circ}{\\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44} \\sin n^\\circ\\sin0.5^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -42px\" width=\"163\" height=\"93\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff3bf21350e6858e229651db44bdecc1490c2ee0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{\\sum\\limits_{n=46}^{89}\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\cos(n-0.5)^\\circ-\\cos(n+0.5)^\\circ\\right)}{\\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{44}\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\cos(n-0.5)^\\circ-\\cos(n+0.5)^\\circ\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -42px\" width=\"315\" height=\"93\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/5/fa55e6b567d06690dbc6153be75474ccb49c090e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}(\\cos45.5^\\circ-\\cos89.5^\\circ)}{\\frac{1}{2}(\\cos0.5^\\circ-\\cos44.5^\\circ)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"207\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/b/05b35aef1a174e0c45606d38f1beb9eda164f793.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{\\cos45.5^\\circ-\\cos89.5^\\circ}{\\cos0.5^\\circ-\\cos44.5^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"182\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efdaf697cd461bfc063a83512ab07d760cf0ef6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{2\\sin\\left(\\frac{45.5+89.5}{2}\\right)^\\circ\\sin\\left(\\frac{45.5-89.5}{2}\\right)^\\circ}{2\\sin\\left(\\frac{0.5+44.5}{2}\\right)^\\circ\\sin\\left(\\frac{0.5-44.5}{2}\\right)^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"262\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/2/462934ddfa3c849f8ecf6cb59261fe1b183a71e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{2\\sin\\frac{135}{2}^\\circ\\sin(-22)^\\circ}{2\\sin\\frac{45}{2}^\\circ\\sin(-22)^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"173\" height=\"51\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/1/da1f0898a6e93d06d543c964f1777aecd9609627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{\\sin\\frac{135}{2}^\\circ}{\\sin\\frac{45}{2}^\\circ}=\\tan\\frac{135}{2}^\\circ=\\frac{1+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}}{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}}=1+\\sqrt{2}\\approx 2.4142$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"410\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/2/9129da27324b6984dfbb0173a74f0dcf06f4d4a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow 100x\\approx 241.42\\Rightarrow\\boxed{241}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"204\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~eevee9406\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Video Solution by Osman Nal:\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o6udScV0F_o\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o6udScV0F_o</a>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME\" title=\"1997 AIME\">1997 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1997 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1997\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1997 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td al